records.body:
Parent: #12
Prerequisite: #59

Purpose: remove normal-path global/linear registration and neighbour lookup while preserving deterministic hierarchical geometry.

Scope:
- stable pool records plus a height-bounded balanced ordered index over canonical discovery-tile keys;
- deterministic canonical traversal independent of allocation/tree rotation;
- incarnation-qualified direct handles for World paths that already know their owner;
- checked signed-coordinate neighbour derivation and boundary-run mapping;
- trusted World-geometry specialization;
- bounded compatibility index for the generic arbitrary-rectangle adapter, using the reviewed row-interval ordered design unless an equivalently proved structure is preferable.

Required tests:
- negative/signed coordinates and endpoint overflow;
- custom and partial geometry;
- forward/reverse insertion;
- capacity refusal;
- generic containment/overlap;
- deterministic traversal;
- optional hash alternative only as a measured cache/control, never the sole worst-case guarantee.

Non-scope: sparse signals, reverse graph dependencies, topology fast paths.

Acceptance: World-canonical registration/facing lookup no longer requires unrelated resident-tile scans, and the generic API still proves non-overlap/containment correctly.

Parent: #12
Prerequisites: #60, #58

Purpose: replace resident observer refresh for material/payload mutations with complete change-driven witness delivery while preserving owner serialization and ABA.

Scope:
- immediate no-allocation invalidation channel;
- deduplicated deferred tile work carrying latest revision/reason;
- direct material/state/temperature mutation hooks;
- movement source and destination;
- Water transfer mutation endpoints where applicable;
- bounded native worker report records;
- deterministic post-barrier reduction;
- lost-report / overflow observation fence;
- coalescing service work without losing change-and-restore history.

Ownership: one integration owner for `native/src/world.cpp` and related producer declarations. Recheck #29/PR #55 immediately before editing; INT-000 semantics remain authoritative and must not be absorbed.

Non-scope: activity/deadline, masks/events/inclusion, graph optimization.

Required tests: direct ABA, exact tuple/heat, render independence, both movement endpoints, same-barrier restore, workers 1/4 parity, signal-record saturation, observer-disabled parity.

Acceptance: direct/worker material changes establish invalidity without a discovery-wide resident scan.

Parent: #12
Prerequisite: #61

Purpose: remove observer-wide polling for no-write activity and future interaction deadlines without changing their blocking semantics.

Scope:
- indexed bounded deadline heap/state keyed canonically by due tick and parent identity;
- at most one current indexed entry per represented parent/kind;
- in-place insert/earlier-replace/cancel/consume;
- parked-excluded overdue state;
- no-write keep-active witness path;
- ordinary sleep/wake transitions;
- re-entry reconciliation;
- no lazy stale-entry accumulation.

Required tests:
- future deadline remains blocking before due;
- earlier replacement, cancellation and consumption;
- equal due-time deterministic order;
- excluded overdue parking/re-entry;
- no-write activity;
- counter/generation exhaustion;
- workers 1/4 parity.

Non-scope: masks/events/inclusion/coverage.

Acceptance: quiet observer maintenance no longer scans every represented discovery tile merely to rediscover unchanged activity/deadline state.

Parent: #12
Prerequisites: #62, #57

Purpose: complete change-driven producer coverage for non-payload conditions that can invalidate settled observations.

Scope:
- exact mask occupancy counts/incidence and set-clear/reconfigure ABA;
- event-to-tile incidence and pending counts using the parent-approved event footprint;
- overlapping-event correctness;
- requested/applied inclusion epochs;
- reservation/chunk/new-coverage notification;
- absence-certificate revocation before new payload becomes consumable;
- explicit coverage states: NotResident, ResidentUntracked, Excluded, Blocked, CapacityRefused, Failed;
- conservative observer-wide quarantine when local coverage integrity cannot be represented.

Non-scope: no event/inclusion physics changes.

Required tests: mask add/remove/reconfigure, overlapping/rejected/drained events, non-default event radius, inclusion request/application, absent→registered-unknown→ready, resident-untracked, tracking-capacity failure, failed-world/reset.

Acceptance: every frozen non-payload producer route has either a sparse exact witness or an explicit safe observation fence.

Parent: #12
Prerequisites: #60, #59

Purpose: replace unrelated graph/global-edge scans with exact local graph incidence and explicit reverse dependency ownership.

Scope:
- one exact capture per tile revision;
- bounded local component extraction;
- revision-bound face runs;
- component incident-edge lists;
- tile→components;
- component→internal domain/current publication;
- publication/build→typed dependencies;
- dependency target→subscribers;
- bounded absence-certificate users;
- immediate logical generation retirement;
- generation-safe deferred cleanup registration.

Keep this primarily inside settled-region graph internals so it can run in parallel with the World producer lane.

Non-scope: topology-preserving/union fast paths, final split scheduler, composable digest.

Required tests: exact tuple/holes, seams, diagonal rejection, new-facing unknown, ready nonmember→matching, absent→resident, stale edge generation, subscriber reuse ABA, component/edge/dependency capacity, immediate old-handle invalidity, far-publication survival.

Acceptance: normal invalidation and edge repair follow actual local incidence/subscriber fanout rather than unrelated global capacity.

Parent: #12
Prerequisites: #63, #64

Purpose: provide the correct generic deletion/split path before any optimization fast path is allowed to hide it.

Scope:
- bounded reconstruction manifests;
- deterministic current exact-graph traversal;
- bounded frontier/visited/dependency state;
- stale-token cancellation and dependency wait states;
- complete-child publication only;
- staged capacity preflight and typed refusal/defer outcomes;
- deterministic admission rounds, retained tickets and positive remote service shares;
- separate cleanup quota and bounded reclamation;
- retry only after relevant dependency/resource-generation change.

Non-scope: topology-preserving/union fast paths.

Required tests: genuine large split, many-child split, alternate-path non-split, mutation of unvisited old member, unknown continuation, mutation during every phase, frontier/dependency/publication exhaustion, sustained local churn with remote work, continuous low-key arrivals, reclamation pressure, slot reuse, no prefix publication.

Acceptance: a large deletion either yields exact complete replacements through bounded service after a stable interval or an honest explicit refusal/defer outcome; unrelated admitted stable work progresses.

Parent: #12
Prerequisite: #65

Purpose: avoid global reconstruction when exact local evidence proves that the affected connectivity relation is preserved or purely additive.

Scope:
- explicit port-equivalence certificate for topology-preserving local replacement;
- internal-hole and equivalent local-change path;
- addition/bridge acceleration;
- deterministic private domain/union machinery where useful;
- canonical member/dependency movement;
- exact fallback to #65 for ambiguity, deletion, changed boundary partition or unknown coverage.

Non-scope: union-find as deletion semantics, topology-continuous public region identity, publication digest redesign.

Required tests: compare every fast path against full exact reconstruction after each edit; unchanged external partition/internal hole; one-cell neck; alternate routes; changed min/bounds; wholly internal components; bridge add/remove; repeated merge/delete epochs.

Acceptance: fast paths are observationally identical to the exact backend and safely fall back whenever their proof is incomplete.

Parent: #12
Prerequisite: #66

Purpose: prevent locally maintained connectivity from becoming globally expensive again solely during publication/certificate preparation.

Scope:
- ordered membership/dependency aggregates;
- aggregate area/bounds/counts and dependency-validity accounting;
- preserve the legacy canonical global fold as the initial compatibility path and explicitly measure its O(m+d) residual work;
- implement a versioned composable diagnostic digest only under the approved staged parent policy;
- specify schema/domain/version tags and canonical sequence semantics;
- keep exact revisions/dependencies as correctness witnesses.

Non-scope: hash equality as connectivity proof.

Required tests: legacy oracle comparison; insertion/allocation/tree-shape independence; canonical member/dependency sequence; local update; global merge; digest-version mismatch; collision/hash equality never substitutes for exact evidence.

Acceptance: publication cost is explicit and measured; any claim of local republication accounts for the selected digest compatibility mode.

Rollback: retain the legacy fold.

Parent: #12
Prerequisite: #56

Purpose: prepare the final evidence campaign independently of the implementation so fixtures, ordering and metrics cannot be selected after seeing candidate results.

Scope:
- Current, Stage-3A and candidate-arm run-plan schema;
- genuine one-cell material/state/temperature fixtures;
- retain historical 8x8 local-edit/full-column bridge controls under their real definitions;
- topology, coverage/absence, deadline/no-write, ABA/fanout, progress/churn, capacity/failure and memory fixtures;
- deterministic workers-1/4 configuration;
- unrestricted-drain and fixed primitive-budget modes;
- balanced preregistered arm ordering;
- minimum five sequential process repeats per paired final-campaign cell;
- raw/provenance schema retaining failures, refusals, timeouts and incomplete jobs;
- reducer/reporting logic without candidate-specific thresholds.

Avoid PR #55's MicroScenario/workbench files; MS-001 remains optional supplemental integration evidence later.

Non-scope: no candidate semantic implementation and no performance acceptance threshold invented in advance.

Acceptance: a complete candidate-independent run plan can be generated and reviewed before the final Stage-3B candidate exists.

Parent: #12
Prerequisites: #68, #69

Purpose: execute the exact-head registered Stage-3B evidence campaign and return a complete exit packet to the supervising parent. This issue does not self-admit Stage 3B.

Before freezing the candidate:
- re-read current main and all relevant merged/open work;
- reconcile accepted #29 interaction changes without importing INT-000 semantics into discovery;
- ensure one coherent authoritative material/scheduler baseline;
- record exact source, compiler, runtime and artifact identities.

Controls:
- Current/discovery-off;
- untouched Stage 3A;
- runtime-sized Stage-3A-equivalent;
- useful intermediate Stage-3B arms;
- complete candidate.

Required execution:
- workers 1 and 4;
- at least five sequential process repeats per paired cell;
- preregistered balanced ordering;
- complete correctness suites;
- ASan/UBSan and feasible TSan;
- allocation/layout and live/staged/retired memory accounting;
- unrestricted drain and fixed primitive-budget service;
- p50/p95/p99/max where populations support them;
- retain every failure/refusal/timeout/incomplete outcome.

Exit packet must address: safety, producer locality, index locality, memory reconciliation, bounded deletion/service, unrelated remote progress, publication honesty/locality, and evidence quality.

Optional MS-001 scenarios are supplemental only after their source/runtime identities are fixed.

Acceptance: publish the parent-owned Stage-3B exit review and raw evidence identities. Final admission remains a separate supervising-parent decision; Stage 4 remains blocked.
